From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: randomkid2 <jayden.mattsson101@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 17:40:00 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] Remove the duplicate STRPRODUCTVER definition

revision.h.in defined STRPRODUCTVER twice. The second definition silently won,
so the first was dead, and a duplicate object-like macro whose replacement lists
differ is a constraint violation that a stricter compiler is entitled to reject.

The surviving definition is the one that was already in effect, so nothing the
application displays changes: About still reads "3.<count>+ [<sha>]".

Signed-off-by: randomkid2 <jayden.mattsson101@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/revision.h.in b/revision.h.in
index 92da9ae..b1fbe69 100644
--- a/revision.h.in
+++ b/revision.h.in
@@ -2,5 +2,4 @@
 
 #pragma once
 
-#define STRPRODUCTVER "3.@NOGGIT_GIT_VERSION_STRING@"
 #define STRPRODUCTVER "3.@NOGGIT_COMMIT_COUNT@ [@NOGGIT_GIT_VERSION_STRING@]"
-- 
2.43.0

